has provided a solution for a large-scale, online KG-based Data-to-Text system. In this paper, we present a novel approach to generating natural sentences from KG triples that can be used for conversational speech recognition. We consider the problem using the large-scale, online KG-based Data-to-Text system we developed as part of our previous work. Our approach consists of two parts: (1) an in-memory KG data structure for storing the KG triples and (2) an out-of-memory KG data structure for storing the words that are to be generated from the KG triples. We show that our approach is efficient and scales well. We also provide a demonstration of our approach.

